# Copy to `.env` in the repo root; docker compose reads it automatically and it
# overrides the defaults in docker-compose.yml / docker/docker-compose.gs.yaml.
# It is gitignored, because every console laptop answers these differently.

# --- console hardware --------------------------------------------------------
# The joystick board and the button board are identical CH340 devices, so the
# /dev/ttyACM* numbering is just kernel enumeration order and it changes across
# reboots and replugs. Pointing the nodes at a fixed ACM number is how the
# sticks end up silent while the switches still work: serial_joy_node opens
# whichever board happens to be ACM0 that boot, finds no frames matching its
# line format, and publishes nothing without ever failing.
#
# Address them by USB serial instead, which follows the board:
#
#   ls -l /dev/serial/by-id/
#
# and identify which is which by reading them - the joystick board streams
# `<9 switch bits>|<6 axis values>` at 921600.
#JOY_BOARD_PORT=/dev/serial/by-id/usb-1a86_USB_Single_Serial_XXXXXXXXXX-if00
#BUTTON_BOARD_PORT=/dev/serial/by-id/usb-1a86_USB_Single_Serial_XXXXXXXXXX-if00

# --- link --------------------------------------------------------------------
#ROVER_LINK_PREFIX=10.44.0.
#ROVER_PEER=10.42.0.1
#MAST_HOST=10.44.0.1
